{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "dialogue_target" %}
{% set dac_ally = is_in_faction(actorUUID, "DAC_AllyFaction") %}
{% if dac_ally %}

{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{% if actorUUID != player.UUID %}
{{ "## You Chose Them" }}
{{ decnpc(actorUUID).name }} sided with {{ player.name }}. Whoever they used to answer to, that is over - they made a choice, and it was for {{ player.name }}.

This is not friendship out of nowhere and it is not servitude. {{ decnpc(actorUUID).name }} is not a follower and takes no orders; they simply will not raise a hand to {{ player.name }}, and would sooner see them get away with it than not. Whatever they wanted out of the arrangement - safety, a share, spite towards their old company, or something they have not said out loud - it is still theirs to want.

If their former people are nearby, {{ decnpc(actorUUID).name }} has a problem, and knows it.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if render_mode == "dialogue_target" %}
{% if responseTarget and responseTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}
{{ "## Your Ally" }}
{{ player.name }} is the person {{ decnpc(actorUUID).name }} threw in with. Whatever else is true, they are not enemies, and both of them know what that cost.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{# Defeat and Capture - personal allies.
   Deliberately NOT gated on captivity: an ally outlives the captivity that
   created them, and most of the interesting conversation happens afterwards.

   Three things write DAC_AllyFaction, and nothing else does:
     1. the player, via the Mark Ally power;
     2. a mercy release with "captors stay friendly" set;
     3. the AI, via the dac_becomeally action (AI_BecomeAlly).

   Route 3 was added after this file and is deliberately narrow: the actor must
   already be in DAC_TruceFaction, so only someone actually holding the player
   can defect, and it takes a real action call. What is still ruled out is the
   model NARRATING a change of heart and being believed - saying "I am with you
   now" writes nothing. That distinction is the point, not "the AI cannot become
   an ally", which it can.

   Kept separate from 5000_capture_state.prompt because the two describe
   different things and can both be true: an ally can be standing in the room
   while the player is still someone else's prisoner. #}
